      "leg": "ours",
      "listing": "Every phone on Earth showed the same patch notes at once, version number and all, for a game nobody installed. One line nerfed whatever used to keep monsters out of buildings. Now there are stairs under Owen's apartment block going down into a dungeon, a status window he cannot close, and things that climb up at night and drop loot that works. Owen tests games for a living. He goes down scared, with a crowbar and a notebook full of repro steps, because two rules in that changelog contradict each other. He wants to reach that gap first, before the guilds forming across town read the wording as carefully as he does.\n",
